pretty interesting. Two states away in Wyoming,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:45.600
Republican lawmakers are looking to go in&nbsp;
a different direction, writes Newsweek,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.640
pushing legislation that would ban the&nbsp;
sale of all new electric vehicles in what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:55.680
lawmakers are calling an effort to preserve&nbsp;
the state's fossil fuel industry. What?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:01.020
Sponsored by Casper, Republican Senator Jim&nbsp;
Anderson. With the support of other Republicans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:09.900
the resolution proposes to phase out the sale of&nbsp;
all new electric vehicles in the state by 2035 to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:16.080
help maintain the fossil fuel jobs that underpin&nbsp;
the state's economy. Imagine I have contraband. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:22.020
went to another state to get it. What is it? Is it&nbsp;
is it meth? What is it? Is it the abortion pill?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:30.180
No, it's an electric vehicle. Huh. That's pretty&nbsp;
bonkers. The proliferation of electric vehicles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:36.420
reads the resolution at the expense of gas powered&nbsp;
vehicles will have a deleterious and will have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:42.120
deleterious impacts on Wyoming's communities and&nbsp;
will be detrimental to Wyoming's economy and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:47.820
ability for the country to efficiently engage in&nbsp;
commerce. They're just going to say you can't buy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:53.580
electric vehicles anymore. Not new. Engadget&nbsp;
reporting Wyoming wants to phase out sales of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.580 --> 00:02:00.540
new EVs by 2035. It's a symbolic gesture aimed&nbsp;
at states like California, California, New York,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:03.900
of course, are going in the direction of saying&nbsp;
after a certain date, we're not going to allow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:08.580
ICE vehicles, internal combustion engine vehicles&nbsp;
to be sold. So a couple of thoughts. First of all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:13.020
this is not exactly the free market. Now,&nbsp;
you could say electric vehicles shouldn't be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:16.440
subsidized. You could say that you could take&nbsp;
that. You could make that argument and say,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:23.280
listen, I really want a free market. So the&nbsp;
government shouldn't offer rebates or tax&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:28.500
credits on electric vehicles. Now, if that's your&nbsp;
position, you should also say that the government&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:34.140
shouldn't subsidize oil and gas fossil fuels at&nbsp;
all. Right. If your position is no subsidies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:39.120
let the free market decide. You've got to get&nbsp;
rid of all subsidies and tax credits. That is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:46.620
certainly one position, but it is not a free&nbsp;
market to, say phase out electric vehicles, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:52.680
continue subsidizing oil and gas, which is exactly&nbsp;
what they want to do. Now, you can make arguments&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:57.420
about electric vehicles that I think are perfectly&nbsp;
fair arguments to make, like, for example, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.420 --> 00:03:02.880
sourcing of some of the materials required to make&nbsp;
batteries is a problem. I'm with you. It's got to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:08.460
be figured out. There is no doubt. I believe it's&nbsp;
cobalt. The sourcing of cobalt for batteries is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:14.880
problem. We have to figure out what do we do with&nbsp;
spent electric vehicle batteries. That question is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:18.960
being answered. It's being worked on. It's going&nbsp;
to be figured out. But you have to remember that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:24.060
there are some systemic, fundamental advantages&nbsp;
to electric vehicles over gas powered vehicles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:31.080
that make this. I would never say this is the end&nbsp;
point. Once electric vehicles are predominant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:36.840
there will be some next thing, right? 100 years,&nbsp;
two, three, 500 years. This isn't the end. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:41.820
when you compare electric to gas powered, gas&nbsp;
powered vehicles typically have what's called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:47.940
energy conversion efficiency of 20%. That means&nbsp;
20% of the energy stored in the gasoline before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:54.180
you burn it is actually used to power the vehicle&nbsp;
20%. That's very low. Electric vehicles have an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.180 --> 00:04:01.320
energy conversion efficiency of 90%, meaning&nbsp;
that 90% of the energy stored in the batteries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:08.400
is actually used to power the vehicle, to power&nbsp;
its systems to move the vehicle at the base level.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:15.720
Electric vehicles are way more efficient at using&nbsp;
energy and they produce fewer emissions. Now then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:21.000
you get to the next layer benefit. Electric&nbsp;
vehicles don't have a tailpipe. They don't emit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:26.400
pollutants and greenhouse gases at the tailpipe.&nbsp;
Gas powered vehicles, as they drive around,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:32.640
spew dangerous pollutants like carbon&nbsp;
monoxide, nitrogen oxides, particulate matter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:36.600
all sorts of stuff. Terrible for human health,&nbsp;
terrible for the environment. Electric vehicles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:40.980
don't do that. There's no tailpipe emissions. They&nbsp;
don't directly pollute the air. Now, of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:45.360
where is the electricity coming from?&nbsp;
The electricity may be polluting the air,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:53.040
but you can get off of that. You can power your&nbsp;
electric vehicle with solar energy, with wind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.040 --> 00:05:00.780
energy. And so every time you go up, up, up the&nbsp;
chain, you reduce the emissions. And the benefit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:05.520
of electric vehicles over gas powered vehicles&nbsp;
grows. Now, we still have problems to solve,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:13.620
